content.text:
Implemented the deterministic package-generator core.

It now:

- accepts a policy-supplied price ladder;
- enumerates valid allowed term combinations;
- calculates full buyer cost `C`;
- enforces must-haves;
- excludes packages worse than the buyer alternative by default;
- returns up to three distinct price/term packages with auditable evaluations and rationales.

Changed:

- [Package generator](/home/stefan/dev/hackathon/slavs-and-a-ottman/negotiator/packages.py)
- [Public module exports](/home/stefan/dev/hackathon/slavs-and-a-ottman/negotiator/__init__.py)
- [Tests](/home/stefan/dev/hackathon/slavs-and-a-ottman/tests/test_packages.py)
- [README](/home/stefan/dev/hackathon/slavs-and-a-ottman/README.md)

Verification: 91 passed, 1 skipped, 20 subtests passed; Ruff is clean.

This is intentionally not wired into an agent yet. The next logical step is the supplier-profile/hypothesis component, then connect that profile to price-ladder selection and this generator.

